    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` feature following the existing `bulkSignupWarning` pattern. The hard rejection at 50 (`RequireCityCapacity` \u2192 409) is untouched.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `capacityWarning` boolean to the owner response schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it; MapStruct maps it by name automatically).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `capacity_warning` column field with getter/setter.\n- **`FlagCapacityWarning.java`** (new) \u2014 counts existing owners in the owner's city (same case-insensitive/trimmed normalization as `RequireCityCapacity`) and sets `capacityWarning = count >= 40 && count < 50`. It runs after `BuildOwner` and before `SaveOwner`, so the owner being created isn't counted.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `capacityWarning` step into the transactional pipeline between `bulkSignup` and `save`.\n- **Schema files** (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `capacity_warning BOOLEAN` column.\n- **`hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 the seed owner rows use positional `INSERT`s, so I added the corresponding `NULL` to each of the 10 rows (h2/postgres use explicit column lists and needed no change; mysql has no owner seed rows).\n\nTest result: `coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` passes, and the full suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
